        "content": "## Scenario B: What to Watch\n\nWith **total rate = 500 msg/s** split equally across N partitions:\n\n- **Throughput** should stay ~500 msg/s regardless of partition count (single drain goroutine)\n- **Latency** will increase with partition count as more goroutines compete for the 100-message channel\n- **Goroutines** = `partitions + 3` (verify via pprof: `curl http://localhost:6060/debug/pprof/goroutine?debug=1`)\n\n### Run commands\n```bash\n# 4 partitions at 125 msg/s each\nfor i in 1 2 3 4; do\n  ./bench-producer -topic bench-p4 -rate 125 -msg-size 1024 -duration 180 &\ndone\n```\n\n### Expected finding\nAdding more partitions does **not** increase throughput — it only increases burst tolerance via the 100-message buffer.",
