        "content": "## Scenario D: Size Scaling\n\nRun these commands in sequence, each for 3 minutes:\n\n```bash\n# 100 B\n./bench-producer -topic bench-p1 -rate 100 -msg-size 100 -duration 180 -shape flat\n\n# 1 KB\n./bench-producer -topic bench-p1 -rate 100 -msg-size 1024 -duration 180 -shape flat\n\n# 10 KB\n./bench-producer -topic bench-p1 -rate 100 -msg-size 10240 -duration 180 -shape flat\n\n# 100 KB\n./bench-producer -topic bench-p1 -rate 100 -msg-size 102400 -duration 180 -shape flat\n```\n\n### What to measure\n- Throughput from `bench-lag-monitor.sh` (offset delta/s)\n- Plugin RSS from `bench-resource-monitor.sh`\n- Panel update smoothness (does it stutter at 100 KB?)\n\n### Expected finding\nJSON decode throughput is 194–279 MB/s — not a bottleneck. Plugin RSS grows proportionally to in-flight message size.",
