        "content": "## Benchmark Topic Reference\n\n| Topic | Partitions | Used in | Panel |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `bench-p1` | 1 | Scenario A (throughput), D (size) | Row 1, Row 4 |\n| `bench-p2` | 2 | Scenario B (partition scaling) | Row 2 |\n| `bench-p4` | 4 | Scenario B | Row 2 |\n| `bench-p8` | 8 | Scenario B | Row 2 |\n| `bench-p16` | 16 | Scenario B | Row 2 |\n| `bench-json` | 1 | Scenario C (format comparison) | Row 3 |\n| `bench-plain` | 1 | Scenario C | Row 3 |\n\n## Create all topics (run once after stack starts)\n\n```bash\nfor P in 1 2 4 8 16; do\n  docker exec kafka /opt/bitnami/kafka/bin/kafka-topics.sh \\\n    --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \\\n    --create --topic bench-p$P --partitions $P --replication-factor 1\ndone\nfor FMT in json avro proto plain; do\n  docker exec kafka /opt/bitnami/kafka/bin/kafka-topics.sh \\\n    --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \\\n    --create --topic bench-$FMT --partitions 1 --replication-factor 1\ndone\n```\n\n## Start monitors before every scenario\n\n```bash\n# Terminal A\n./bench-lag-monitor.sh bench-p1 5\n\n# Terminal B  \n./bench-resource-monitor.sh 5\n```\n\n## pprof during peak load\n\n```bash\ngo tool pprof -http :8888 http://localhost:6060/debug/pprof/profile?seconds=30   # CPU\ngo tool pprof -http :8889 http://localhost:6060/debug/pprof/heap                  # heap\ngo tool pprof -http :8890 http://localhost:6060/debug/pprof/mutex                 # lock overhead\n```",
